here of least area $r = 0$, between the two horizons, to a finite $(9r_s^2 - 16ar_s + 12a^2)/a^6$, which is $256/r_s^4$ here. $K$ depends on $r$ through the areal radius $\\rho = \\sqrt{r^2 + a^2}$ alone, so it is the same at $r$ and at $-r$, and it falls from $r = 0$ outward on both sides. It lies below Schwarzschild's out to $r = 4.428\\,r_s$ and above it beyond, and far out approaches it as $12r_s^2/r^6 + 16a^2r_s/r^7$.","On the sphere of least area $r = 0$, $R = (3r_s - 2a)/a^3 = 16/r_s^2$. In the areal radius $\\rho = \\sqrt{r^2 + a^2}$, $R = -a^2(2\\rho - 3r_s)/\\rho^5$, which changes sign where $\\rho = 3r_s/2$, at $r = \\pm 1.414\\,r_s$, outside the horizons. It is least, $-0.00809/r_s^2$, where $\\rho = 15r_s/8$, at $r = \\pm 1.807\\,r_s$, and far out falls off as $-2a^2/r^4$."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the black bounce against $r$ ($a = r_s/2$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, beside Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3}$ and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.478\\,r_s$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","$K$ of Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass"],["line","horizon","a horizon, where $g^{rr} = 0$"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R$ of the black bounce against $r$ ($a = r_s/2$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $R\\,r_s^2$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $0.001$ of zero, from $-1$ to $10^{2}$; no curve leaves its panel.","legend":[["line","R","$R$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","horizon","a horizon, where $g^{rr} = 0$"]]}},"settings":"$r_s = 1$, the unit of every length, and $a = r_s/2$, so that $r_\\pm = \\pm\\sqrt{r_s^2 - a^2} = \\pm 0.866\\,r_s$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3