depends on $r$ through the areal radius $\\rho = \\sqrt{r^2 + a^2}$ alone, so it is the same at $r$ and at $-r$, and it falls from the throat outward on both sides. It lies below Schwarzschild's out to $r = 4.243\\,r_s$ and above it beyond, and far out approaches it as $12r_s^2/r^6 + 16a^2r_s/r^7$.","On the throat $r = 0$, $R = (3r_s - 2a)/a^3 = 1/r_s^2$. In the areal radius $\\rho = \\sqrt{r^2 + a^2}$, $R = -a^2(2\\rho - 3r_s)/\\rho^5$, which changes sign where $\\rho = 3r_s/2$, at $r = \\pm 1.118\\,r_s$. It is least, $-0.0324/r_s^2$, where $\\rho = 15r_s/8$, at $r = \\pm 1.586\\,r_s$, and far out falls off as $-2a^2/r^4$."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the one way wormhole against $r$ ($a = r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, beside Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3}$ and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.478\\,r_s$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","$K$ of Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R$ of the one way wormhole against $r$ ($a = r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $R\\,r_s^2$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $0.001$ of zero, from $-1$ to $10^{2}$; no curve leaves its panel.","legend":[["line","R","$R$, the Ricci scalar"]]}},"settings":"$r_s = 1$, the unit of every length, and $a = r_s$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3}$ and $R\\,r_s^2$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $0.001$ of zero, from $-1$ to $10^{2}$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.478\\,r_s$."},{"id":"wormhole","label":"$a = 2\\,r_s$","kind":"line","x":{"name":"$r/r_s$","from":-4,"to":4,"ticks":[{"at":-4.0,"label":