^2 - 16ar_s + 12a^2)/a^6$, which is $0.391/r_s^4$ here, and toward $r = 0$ Schwarzschild's $K = 12r_s^2/r^6$ grows without bound. $K$ depends on $r$ through $\\rho$ alone, so it is the same at $r$ and at $-r$, and it falls from the throat outward on both sides. It lies below Schwarzschild's out to $r = 3.858\\,r_s$ and above it beyond, and far out approaches it as $12r_s^2/r^6 + 16a^2r_s/r^7$.","In the areal radius $\\rho = \\sqrt{r^2 + a^2}$, $R = -a^2(2\\rho - 3r_s)/\\rho^5$, negative at every $r$, since $\\rho \\ge a > 3r_s/2$. It is least on the throat, $(3r_s - 2a)/a^3 = -0.125/r_s^2$, rises toward zero on both sides, and far out falls off as $-2a^2/r^4$."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the traversable wormhole against $r$ ($a = 2\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, beside Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3}$ and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.478\\,r_s$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","$K$ of Schwarzschild's black hole of the same mass"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R$ of the traversable wormhole against $r$ ($a = 2\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$.","clip":"We draw $R\\,r_s^2$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $0.001$ of zero, from $-1$ to $10^{2}$; no curve leaves its panel.","legend":[["line","R","$R$, the Ricci scalar"]]}},"settings":"$r_s = 1$, the unit of every length, and $a = 2\\,r_s$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-3}$ to $10^{3}$ and $R\\,r_s^2$ on a signed logarithmic scale, linear within $0.001$ of zero, from $-1$ to $10^{2}$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.478\\,r_s$."}]}
